      "answer": "The sovereignty of the Falkland Islands is a long-standing dispute between the United Kingdom and Argentina. The United Kingdom administers the islands and maintains that the Falkland Islanders have the right to self-determination, a position supported by a 2013 referendum in which the vast majority of residents voted to remain a British Overseas Territory. Argentina, however, claims the islands (which it calls the Malvinas) as an integral part of its national territory, arguing that they were illegally occupied by Britain. Consequently, how one interprets the status of the islands often depends on whether one prioritizes the principle of self-determination for the local population or the territorial claims asserted by Argentina.",
